  "id": "COMPOUND:118 - PROTEIN:1026",
  "verbalization": "Spermine is implicated in the regulation of Cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor 1 through multiple pathways, with the core mechanism involving its interaction with DNA gyrase subunit B and other enzymes. The evidence suggests that Spermine acts as a target for various compounds, including [(1S,2S,4R,7E,10R,11R)-4,8-dimethyl-12-methylidene-13-oxo-3,14-dioxatricyclo[9.3.0.02,4]tetradec-7-en-10-yl] acetate and 3-anhydro-6-hydroxy-ophiobolin A, which both target Cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor 1. These compounds are known to inhibit cyclin-dependent kinases, and their interaction with Spermine suggests a potential role in modulating the activity of these kinases. The presence of multiple independent pathways linking Spermine to Cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor 1 underscores the complexity of the relationship, but the consistent targeting of the same downstream target (Cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor 1) across different compounds supports a mechanistic link. The evidence is robust, but the exact nature of the interaction between Spermine and the kinase inhibitor remains to be fully elucidated.",
